WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.770
- Wait, so speaking of
friends coming to a show,

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.420
I always tell people to never tell me

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.800
if someone comes to a show.
- Oh, really?

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.030
- Yeah, I hate knowing.

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:07.740
Do you like knowing?

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.120
- Well, in a long run like this,

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.710
where you're doing the same show.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.603
we've done it 110 times now,

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:16.290
it helps me to see it through new eyes.

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:17.370
- Oh, okay.
- I can get excited

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:18.810
'cause I know so-and-so's out there,

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.483
and they're English, so
they'll hate my accent.

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:23.363
- They're judging.

00:00:23.363 --> 00:00:24.303
- Or they're really judgy

00:00:24.303 --> 00:00:25.830
so they'll hate the whole show.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.530
- Oh man, I don't get nervous on stage,

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:30.480
but when I know that friends
are family or something's,

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.250
I'm like, "I don't wanna know."

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.410
- I don't know why it
gives me a little kick.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:35.730
- So one time, speaking of that though,

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:37.410
you actually surprised Sean Hayes, right?

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:38.250
Was in Chicago?

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.860
- Yeah, so Sean, if, I
dunno if you got a chance

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:41.880
to see "Goodnight Oscar,"

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.291
but he won the Tony for it this year.

00:00:43.291 --> 00:00:44.124
- [Kelly] He's so talented.

00:00:44.124 --> 00:00:46.560
- He's so incredible.
- And sweet.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.393
- There's us together.

00:00:47.393 --> 00:00:52.393
But he did it in Chicago first
and I knew he was doing it,

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:55.140
it was very low key, this
is like year and a half ago.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.600
But I flew in to see him and surprise him

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.317
and I told him that night,

00:00:59.317 --> 00:01:00.360
"You're going to New York, right?"

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.193
He said, "Yeah, hopefully."

00:01:01.193 --> 00:01:03.390
And I said, "Yeah, you're
gonna win the Tony."

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:04.350
- Oh my God.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:06.840
You're like Nostradamus,
you predicted that.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:07.673
- It was pretty clear.

00:01:07.673 --> 00:01:09.863
He was pretty awesome.
- Yeah, he's so talented.

